      "id": 34167,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-07-19T12:17:09.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;evandan55&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"evandan55\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don’t trust any villain.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That’s probably a good call. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>Yeah, the cards that come up really make a huge difference, as do the heroes involved. Obviously, the environment will change things up. We went against Advanced Omnitron Tuesday and had very few issues, but then we had a good combination of heroes that allowed us to manage the situation very well, his cards ran cold, and Insala Primalis’s Velociraptors were eating Drones left and right. ;D</p>\n<p>(We poured butter on the Drones. At least that’s my story, and I’m sticking to it. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> )</p>",
