      "username": "clarinetnerd",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/77aa72/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-07-22T09:31:32.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;ketigid&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"ketigid\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Any epic fail stories of how the heroes were overwhelming the villain and decided to take it easy (and not finish the villain off when they can already do it and maybe let the Police Backup or Kraken or something deal the finishing blow), only to have the villain bounce right back and wipe the floor with the heroes?</p>\n<p>Any? <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>OH yes!  Our group was being cool and tried to get 3 Story Challenges done at once.  We wanted to heal for 5+ in one turn (we decided to use the pillars to do that), and win with both the pillars and the Atlantean Font of Power in play.  FALSE.  We ended up doing the healing with the Pillars out and the Font next in the environment deck thanks to Visionary.  We decided to leave the pillars for one more turn…  Then Omnitron kicked out behinds as he continued to play more cards.  Whoops!</p>",
